    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d486-a2">

                <pb facs="0613" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg505"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 30—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The minister for foreign affairs to Mr.
                    McDonald.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran, Persia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-26"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of the
                    “petition” which your excellency, in your communication of the 7th of
                    Rabi-es-sani, desired me to lay before His Imperial Majesty, and to inform you
                    that a reply will be sent through his highness the prime minister to your
                    excellency.</p>
                <p>I beg to repeat, etc.</p>
                <closer>[Seal of the Kavamed Doulah, minister for foreign affairs.]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
